+
+## Background
+
+Axiathon needs a unified extensibility layer so that all data source integrations, protocol dissectors, notification channels, and response actions follow the same SDK, manifest format, packaging, and lifecycle management. Without this, each extension point would require its own tooling, creating maintenance burden and inconsistency for both platform developers and third-party plugin authors.
+
+The spike workspace (`spike/crates/axiathon-plugin-sdk/`) has a complete, tested plugin SDK with 5 sub-crates (core, ingestion, network, notification, action), 6 plugin types, and 6 working first-party plugins. This epic ports the spike to production with key improvements: structured `PluginError` (replacing anyhow), extended `PluginManifest` (config_schema, OCSF metadata, signatures), JSON Schema config validation, and WASM sandboxing via Extism.
+
+### Requirements Coverage
+
+- **FR314-FR338:** Protocol Dissector SDK (plugin architecture, WASM sandbox)
+- **FR339-FR394:** Ingestion Plugin System (Parser, Connector, Enricher, OCSF extensions, DSL fields, asset discovery, dependency management)
+- **NFR172-NFR173:** Parser performance (Native 10us/line, WASM 100us/line)
+- **NFR174-NFR175:** Plugin lifecycle (load <1s, hot-reload <5s)
+- **NFR176-NFR177:** Connector performance (50K events/s, health checks <5s)
+- **NFR178-NFR180:** Enricher performance (10ms/event sync, 1K events/500ms batch, 1ms cache)
+- **NFR181-NFR182:** Custom field resolution (OCSF <100us, DSL <500us overhead)
+- **NFR183:** Plugin registry supports 100+ concurrent plugins
+
+## Technical Architecture
+
+### SDK Workspace Structure
+
+The plugin SDK lives at `crates/axiathon-plugin-sdk/` with 6 crates registered as root workspace members (Cargo does not support nested workspaces):
+
+```
+crates/axiathon-plugin-sdk/
+  Cargo.toml                    # Facade crate re-exporting all sub-crates
+  src/lib.rs                    # pub use axiathon_plugin_sdk_{core,ingestion,network,notification,action}
+  core/                         # AxiathonPlugin base trait, PluginManifest, PluginId, PluginKind, PluginError
+  ingestion/                    # LogParser, SourceConnector, EventEnricher traits
+  network/                      # ProtocolDissector trait
+  notification/                 # NotificationChannel trait
+  action/                       # ResponseAction trait
+```
+
+### Trait Hierarchy
+
+All plugin types extend `AxiathonPlugin` (base trait with manifest, initialize, health_check, shutdown). Type-specific traits add domain methods:
+
+- `LogParser` -- `detect()`, `parse()`, `schema()` (sync, no async_trait)
+- `SourceConnector` -- `connect()`, `collect()` returning `BoxStream<RawLogLine>` (async_trait for dyn dispatch)
+- `EventEnricher` -- `enrich()` with in-place mutation, `cache_config()`, `priority()` (async_trait for dyn dispatch)
+- `ProtocolDissector` -- `can_dissect()`, `dissect()` (sync, no async_trait)
+- `NotificationChannel` -- `send()`, `test_connection()` (async_trait for dyn dispatch)
+- `ResponseAction` -- `execute()`, `validate_params()` (async_trait for dyn dispatch)
+
+### Two-Tier Registry Model
+
+- **Global `UnifiedPluginRegistry`:** Stores plugin binaries, manifests, and metadata. Shared across tenants.
+- **Tenant `TenantPluginRegistry`:** Per-tenant plugin instances with tenant-scoped configuration. References global binary (not copied).
+- **FirstPartyPluginPolicy:** Controls which built-in plugins are auto-available per tenant.
+
+### Plugin Lifecycle
+
+Discover -> Validate -> Register -> Configure -> Activate -> Monitor. Signature verification runs during validation (strict/warn/disabled per config).
+
+### WASM Sandbox (Extism)
+
+Multi-language plugin support (Python, Go, JavaScript, C) via Extism WASM host. Memory isolation per plugin, fuel-based execution limits, blocked WASI imports (no file/socket/proc_exit). Performance target: <100us/line (10x native overhead budget).
+
+### Packaging
+
+`.axpkg` is a ZIP archive containing: manifest.yaml, plugin.wasm, plugin.wasm.sig, README.md, LICENSE. GPG detached signatures with offline verification. `.axpkgs` is a TAR bundle for air-gap transfer.
+
